s<url>","medium_element_one_cookie":"To view <%=componentname%>, <url>adjust your <%=cookietype%> cookie settings.<url>","medium_element_two_cookie":"To view <%=componentname%>, <url>adjust your <%=cookietype%> and <%=cookietype%> cookie settings.<url>","small_element_one_cookie":"<url>Update your cookie settings<url>","small_element_two_cookie":"<url>Update your cookie settings<url>","small_tooltip_one_cookie":"To view <%=componentname%>, update your <%=cookietype%> settings.","small_tooltip_two_cookie":"To view <%=componentname%>, update your <%=cookietype%> and <%=cookietype%> settings.","small_element_aria_label":"More info","tiny_element_one_cookie":"<%=componentname%> was blocked due to your <%=cookietype%> cookie settings. <url>Update your settings<url>","tiny_element_two_cookie":"<%=componentname%> was blocked due to your <%=cookietype%> and <%=cookietype%> cookie settings. <url>Update your settings<url>","tiny_element_aria_label":"Unblock <%=componentname%>","analytics":"analytics","functional":"functional","essential":"essential","advertising":"marketing"}},"comp-kwmluvcz":{"html":"<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:14px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">You can make this Chanterelle Chowder with any variety of Chanterelles you may have including winter Chanterelles also known as Yellow Foot. These are much smaller but also delicious. Of course you can use this chowder recipe for any other mushroom or veggie or even clams!</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:14px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:14px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">The interesting thing about using chanterelles for chowder is that they really do tend to look and feel like clams when prepared this way, chopped into small pieces of similar size of course.</span></p>","skin":"WRichTextNewSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"},"comp-kwmluvd1":{"translations":{"title":"Widget Didn’t Load","text1":"Check your internet and refresh this page.","text2":"If that doesn’t work, contact us."}},"comp-kwmluvd8":{"html":"<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">I also use an 8 oz bottle of clam juice to enhance the flavor likeness. You can use another liquid if you&#39;d rather not use the clam juice. I would suggest a broth, dry white wine or milk.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">When it comes to adding the cream, I use fat free half and half but feel free to use full on whipping cream or regular half and half. When using milk either whole, 2%, 1% or skim, the chowder tends to be too thin and less white for my taste but it does work. Evaporated milk will also work here but I notice a distinct difference in taste when using it. I&#39;ve never tried to use a milk alternative like, soy, oat or almond before.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:14px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">I like to add half of the celery at the start to add flavor to the creamy soup base then add in more chopped celery just before the potatoes. The celery added first will nearly melt away into the soup and later ones will add texture to the chowder without being crunchy.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:14px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">As for the potatoes, a typical PNW chowder is made with russet potatoes. Peel them and chop them, some into small pieces and some into medium pieces. This means they will cook at different rates and the smaller pieces will mostly dissolve into the cream, thickening the chowder while the larger pieces will remain for bite size chunks of creamy deliciousness.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></p>\n\n<p class=\"font_8 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Here is a step by step look at how I put this chowder together. Click on the images for more info.</span></p>","skin":"WRichTextNewSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"},"comp-kwmluvda":{"translations":{"title":"Widget Didn’t Load","text1":"Check your internet and refresh this page.","text2":"If that doesn’t work, contact us."}},"comp-kwmluvdc":{"html":"<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">This Chanterelle Chowder recipe is so creamy and comforting!<br class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">\n<br class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">\nI like to garnish any good chowder with a pat of butter, a splash of dry sherry and a sprinkle of crispy bacon bits. It is highly recommend for this Chanterelle Chowder.&nbsp;</span><br class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">\n<br class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">\n<span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Cheers!</span><br class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">\n<span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">~Melisa</span></h5>","skin":"WRichTextNewSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"},"comp-kwmluvdd1":{"translations":{"title":"Widget Didn’t Load","text1":"Check your internet and refresh this page.","text2":"If that doesn’t work, contact us."}},"comp-kwmluvdf":{"html":"<h2 class=\"font_2 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:22px; line-height:1.2em;\"><span style=\"font-size:22px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-family:caudex,serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.09em;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"color:#292929;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">If you enjoyed this post you might like these!</span></span></span></span></span><br class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">\n<br class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">\n<a href=\"https://www.theglasspantry.com/panang-pumpkin-soup\" target=\"_self\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"color:#2B6CA3;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-family:caudex,serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.09em;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-size:20px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Panang Pumpkin Soup</span></span></span></span></span></span></a><br class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">\n<br class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">\n<a href=\"https://www.theglasspantry.com/asparagus-shrimp-and-mushroom-skill\" target=\"_self\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-family:caudex,serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"color:#2B6CA3;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.09em;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-size:20px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Asparagus, Shrimp and Mushroom Skillet</span></span></span></span></span></span></a><br class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">\n<br class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">\n<a href=\"https://www.theglasspantry.com/escargot-stuffed-mushrooms\" target=\"_self\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-family:caudex,serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"color:#2B6CA3;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.09em;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-size:20px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Escargot Stuffed Mushrooms</span></span></span></span></span></span></a><br class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">\n<br class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">\n<a href=\"https://www.theglasspantry.com/grow-blue-oyster-mushrooms\" target=\"_self\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-family:caudex,serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"color:#2B6CA3;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.09em;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-size:20px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Growing Blue Oyster Mushrooms</span></span></span></span></span></span></a><br class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">\n<br class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">\n<a href=\"https://www.theglasspantry.com/french-onion-soup\" target=\"_self\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-family:caudex,serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"color:#2B6CA3;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"letter-spacing:0.09em;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-size:20px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">French Onion Soup</span></span></span></span></span></span></a></h2>","skin":"WRichTextNewSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"},"comp-kwmluvdm":{"crop":{"x":0,"y":19,"width":4032,"height":2987},"alt":"20211117_175712.jpg","width":4032,"height":3024,"uri":"577c92_5acaf873b4c5416baa0045e40d81ee31~mv2.jpg","name":"20211117_175712.jpg","containerId":"comp-kwmluvdm","hasBgScrollEffect":"","bgEffectName":"","displayMode":"fill","link":{},"encoding":"AVIF","allowWebpAvifTransforms":true,"responsiveImageProps":{"fallbackSrc":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/577c92_5acaf873b4c5416baa0045e40d81ee31~mv2.jpg/v1/crop/x_0,y_19,w_4032,h_2987/fill/w_594,h_440,al_c,q_80,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/20211117_175712.jpg","srcset":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/577c92_5acaf873b4c5416baa0045e40d81ee31~mv2.jpg/v1/crop/x_0,y_19,w_4032,h_2987/fill/w_594,h_440,al_c,q_80,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/20211117_175712.jpg 1x, https://static.wixstatic.com/media/577c92_5acaf873b4c5416baa0045e40d81ee31~mv2.jpg/v1/crop/x_0,y_19,w_4032,h_2987/fill/w_1188,h_880,al_c,q_85,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/20211117_175712.jpg 2x","css":{"container":{"position":"relative"},"img":{"width":594,"height":440,"objectFit":"cover"}}},"containerWidth":594,"containerHeight":440,"isInFirstFold":false,"onClickBehavior":"zoomMode","fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WPhoto","language":"en","compId":"comp-kwmluvdm","mainPageId":"qgy49",